# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Background {#background}"
msgstr "Latar Belakang {#background}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This tutorial demonstrates how to implement the Krylov quantum diagonalization (KQD) algorithm within the context of Qiskit patterns.\n"
"You will first learn the theory behind the algorithm and then see a demonstration of its execution on a QPU.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tutorial ini menunjukkan cara melaksanakan algoritma penyepelasan kuantum Krylov (KQD) dalam konteks corak Qiskit.\n"
"Anda akan belajar teori di sebalik algoritma ini terlebih dahulu, kemudian melihat demonstrasi pelaksanaannya pada QPU.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Estimating the low-energy properties of many-body Hamiltonians is a central task in quantum simulation.\n"
"For example, ground-state energies and low-lying excitations are directly related to chemical stability, magnetic ordering, quantum phase transitions, and material response.\n"
"On a classical computer, the Hilbert-space dimension grows exponentially with the number of orbitals or spins, so direct diagonalization quickly becomes impractical.\n"
msgstr ""
"Menganggarkan sifat tenaga-rendah Hamiltonian banyak-jasad adalah tugas utama dalam simulasi kuantum.\n"
"Sebagai contoh, tenaga keadaan-dasar dan pengujaan rendah berkait secara langsung dengan kestabilan kimia, susunan magnet, peralihan fasa kuantum, dan tindak balas bahan.\n"
"Pada komputer klasik, dimensi ruang-Hilbert berkembang secara eksponen dengan bilangan orbital atau spin, jadi pepenjuruan langsung menjadi tidak praktikal dengan cepat.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There are several quantum-computing approaches to this problem.\n"
"Near-term variational methods, such as the [variational quantum eigensolver (VQE)](/tutorials/spin-chain-vqe), use relatively shallow parameterized circuits, but they require a nonlinear classical optimization loop with many quantum-circuit evaluations.\n"
"At the other end, [quantum phase estimation (QPE)](https://arxiv.org/abs/quant-ph/0604193) provides a more direct route to eigenvalue estimation with rigorous guarantees, but standard QPE requires long coherent circuits and is mainly suited to fault-tolerant quantum computers.\n"
"KQD sits between these two approaches: it uses real-time Hamiltonian evolution, as in phase-estimation-based algorithms, but replaces full phase estimation with a compact projected eigenvalue problem that can be solved classically.\n"
msgstr ""
"Terdapat beberapa pendekatan pengkomputeran kuantum untuk masalah ini.\n"
"Kaedah variasi jangka pendek, seperti [variational quantum eigensolver (VQE)](/tutorials/spin-chain-vqe), menggunakan Circuit berparameter yang agak cetek, tetapi ia memerlukan gelung pengoptimuman klasik tak linear dengan banyak penilaian Circuit kuantum.\n"
"Di hujung yang lain, [quantum phase estimation (QPE)](https://arxiv.org/abs/quant-ph/0604193) menyediakan laluan yang lebih langsung untuk anggaran nilai eigen dengan jaminan yang tegas, tetapi QPE piawai memerlukan Circuit koheren yang panjang dan hanya sesuai untuk komputer kuantum toleran-kesalahan.\n"
"KQD berada di antara kedua-dua pendekatan ini: ia menggunakan evolusi Hamiltonian masa-nyata, seperti dalam algoritma berasaskan anggaran-fasa, tetapi menggantikan anggaran fasa penuh dengan masalah nilai eigen terunjur yang padat yang boleh diselesaikan secara klasik.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Consider an $n$-qubit Hamiltonian $H$ and a reference state $\\lvert \\psi_{0}\\rangle$.\n"
"The KQD method builds a Krylov subspace from real-time evolved states,\n"
msgstr ""
"Pertimbangkan Hamiltonian $n$-Qubit $H$ dan keadaan rujukan $\\lvert \\psi_{0}\\rangle$.\n"
"Kaedah KQD membina subruang Krylov daripada keadaan yang berevolusi secara masa-nyata,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\lvert \\psi_\\ell\\rangle = e^{-i\\ell\\Delta t H}\\lvert \\psi_{0}\\rangle,\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\ell = 0,1,\\ldots,r-1,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\lvert \\psi_\\ell\\rangle = e^{-i\\ell\\Delta t H}\\lvert \\psi_{0}\\rangle,\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\ell = 0,1,\\ldots,r-1,\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $r$ is the Krylov dimension and $\\Delta t$ is the time step.\n"
"Any state in the Krylov subspace is then represented as a linear combination of these basis states,\n"
msgstr ""
"dengan $r$ ialah dimensi Krylov dan $\\Delta t$ ialah langkah masa.\n"
"Sebarang keadaan dalam subruang Krylov kemudian diwakili sebagai gabungan linear keadaan asas ini,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\lvert \\psi(\\mathbf{c})\\rangle\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\lvert \\psi(\\mathbf{c})\\rangle\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\frac{\\sum_{\\ell=0}^{r-1} c_\\ell \\lvert \\psi_\\ell\\rangle}\n"
"{\\left\\|\\sum_{\\ell=0}^{r-1} c_\\ell \\lvert \\psi_\\ell\\rangle\\right\\|},\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
"where the denominator normalizes the state.\n"
msgstr ""
"\\frac{\\sum_{\\ell=0}^{r-1} c_\\ell \\lvert \\psi_\\ell\\rangle}\n"
"{\\left\\|\\sum_{\\ell=0}^{r-1} c_\\ell \\lvert \\psi_\\ell\\rangle\\right\\|},\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
"where the denominator normalizes the state.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With simple algebra, we can see that the corresponding energy is written as the Rayleigh quotient,\n"
msgstr "Dengan algebra ringkas, kita boleh melihat bahawa tenaga yang sepadan ditulis sebagai kadar hasil bagi Rayleigh,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"E(\\mathbf{c})\n"
"=\\langle \\psi(\\mathbf{c})|H|\\psi(\\mathbf{c}) \\rangle=\n"
"\\frac{\n"
"\\sum_{k,\\ell} c_k^* c_\\ell \\langle \\psi_k\\vert H\\vert\\psi_\\ell\\rangle\n"
"}{\n"
"\\sum_{k,\\ell} c_k^* c_\\ell \\langle \\psi_k\\vert\\psi_\\ell\\rangle\n"
"}\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"E(\\mathbf{c})\n"
"=\\langle \\psi(\\mathbf{c})|H|\\psi(\\mathbf{c}) \\rangle=\n"
"\\frac{\n"
"\\sum_{k,\\ell} c_k^* c_\\ell \\langle \\psi_k\\vert H\\vert\\psi_\\ell\\rangle\n"
"}{\n"
"\\sum_{k,\\ell} c_k^* c_\\ell \\langle \\psi_k\\vert\\psi_\\ell\\rangle\n"
"}\n"
"=\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\frac{\n"
"\\mathbf{c}^{\\dagger}\\mathcal{H}\\mathbf{c}\n"
"}{\n"
"\\mathbf{c}^{\\dagger}\\mathcal{S}\\mathbf{c}\n"
"}.\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\frac{\n"
"\\mathbf{c}^{\\dagger}\\mathcal{H}\\mathbf{c}\n"
"}{\n"
"\\mathbf{c}^{\\dagger}\\mathcal{S}\\mathbf{c}\n"
"}.\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here, the matrices $\\mathcal{S}$ and $\\mathcal{H}$,\n"
msgstr "Di sini, matriks $\\mathcal{S}$ dan $\\mathcal{H}$,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\mathcal{S}_{k\\ell}=\\langle \\psi_k\\vert\\psi_\\ell\\rangle,\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\mathcal{H}_{k\\ell}=\\langle \\psi_k\\vert H\\vert\\psi_\\ell\\rangle\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\mathcal{S}_{k\\ell}=\\langle \\psi_k\\vert\\psi_\\ell\\rangle,\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\mathcal{H}_{k\\ell}=\\langle \\psi_k\\vert H\\vert\\psi_\\ell\\rangle\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"define the projected overlap and Hamiltonian matrices.\n"
"Their entries are estimated using quantum-circuit measurements.\n"
msgstr ""
"mentakrifkan matriks pertindihan dan Hamiltonian terunjur.\n"
"Entrinya dianggarkan menggunakan pengukuran Circuit kuantum.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We aim to find the coefficient $\\mathbf{c}$ that gives the minimum $E(\\mathbf{c})$:\n"
msgstr "Kami bertujuan mencari pekali $\\mathbf{c}$ yang memberikan $E(\\mathbf{c})$ minimum:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\min_{\\mathbf{c}\\neq \\mathbf{0}} E(\\mathbf{c}).\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\min_{\\mathbf{c}\\neq \\mathbf{0}} E(\\mathbf{c}).\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "By the Rayleigh-Ritz theorem, this minimization is equivalent to solving the generalized eigenvalue problem (GEVP),\n"
msgstr "Berdasarkan teorem Rayleigh-Ritz, peminimuman ini setara dengan menyelesaikan masalah nilai eigen teritlak (GEVP),\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\mathcal{H}\\mathbf{c}=E \\mathcal{S}\\mathbf{c}.\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{equation*}\n"
"\\mathcal{H}\\mathbf{c}=E \\mathcal{S}\\mathbf{c}.\n"
"\\end{equation*}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note that the dimension $r$ can be small enough for a classical computer to solve the GEVP.\n"
msgstr "Ambil perhatian bahawa dimensi $r$ boleh cukup kecil untuk komputer klasik menyelesaikan GEVP.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is the same variational principle used in classical subspace diagonalization, but here the basis states are generated by quantum time evolution.\n"
"Compared with VQE, KQD usually requires deeper circuits because it relies on real-time evolution.\n"
"In return, KQD avoids nonlinear parameter optimization and iterative quantum-hardware execution, and it systematically improves as the projected subspace is enlarged.\n"
"The algorithm has been demonstrated at large scale on existing quantum hardware [\\[2\\]](#references), and its performance can be analyzed with provable guarantees [\\[1\\]](#references).\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini adalah prinsip variasi yang sama yang digunakan dalam pepenjuruan subruang klasik, tetapi di sini keadaan asas dihasilkan oleh evolusi masa kuantum.\n"
"Berbanding VQE, KQD biasanya memerlukan Circuit yang lebih dalam kerana ia bergantung pada evolusi masa-nyata.\n"
"Sebagai balasan, KQD mengelakkan pengoptimuman parameter tak linear dan pelaksanaan perkakasan kuantum berulang, dan ia bertambah baik secara sistematik apabila subruang terunjur diperbesarkan.\n"
"Algoritma ini telah ditunjukkan pada skala besar pada perkakasan kuantum sedia ada [\\[2\\]](#references), dan prestasinya boleh dianalisis dengan jaminan yang boleh dibuktikan [\\[1\\]](#references).\n"

